<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - CANTV raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - CANTV raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- HSBC James Capel raised its rating on CANTV to buy from long-term buy, the brokerage firm said on Monday.</p>
<p>-- HSBC James Capel analysts Jim Noble and Paul Aran cited the Venezuelan government's decision to approve rate increases scheduled for the second quarter for CANTV, the telephone company based in Caracas.</p>
<p>-- The analysts placed a 12-month target on CANTV ADRs at 42. The stock was unchanged at 30-3/4 on Monday.</p>
<p>-- In Caracas, the shares traded up eight bolivars at 2,118.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk 212 859-1730))</p>
</text>
